# Reforger Host Discord bot

## Layout

- Entry: `src/bot/index.ts` — loads config, deploys slash commands, starts client.
- Commands live under `src/bot/commands/<group>/` (e.g. `gen`, `admin`).
- Each command file exports `export const command: BotCommand`.
- Shared command helpers go in `commands/<group>/utils/` (never registered as commands).
- Shared bot utilities go in `src/bot/utils/`.

## Slash command deploy

- Do **not** add a separate deploy script.
- Registration runs on every bot startup via `deployCommands()` in `src/bot/utils/deploy-commands.ts`.

## Agent integration

- Call the host agent through `src/bot/utils/agent.ts` (`agentFetch`), not duplicate HTTP logic.
- Bot credentials load from panel settings (`GET /settings`) via `lib/shared/discord-bot-settings.ts`.
- Reuse shared panel types and embed helpers from `lib/shared/` when possible.

## File size (500 LOC)

- Keep every file under **500 lines**. Split before hitting the limit.
- Extract helpers into `utils/` or `commands/<group>/utils/` and re-import.
- Prefer many small modules over one large command file.

## Practices

- Dashboard-first: prefer read-only embeds (`/dashboard`, `/status`, `/instances`, `/host`) over chat spam.
- Admin-only lifecycle commands (`start`, `stop`, `restart`) must use `adminOnly: true` and `requireAdmin`.
- Handle errors with `utils/errors.ts`; defer replies before agent calls.
- Use discord.js **14.x** APIs (`SlashCommandBuilder`, `REST`, `Routes`).
